  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Vector Calculus and the Stokes Theorems [S+N]\n\nThree differential operators on smooth scalar / vector fields in $\\mathbb{R}^3$:\n\n- **Gradient** $\\nabla f = (\\partial f/\\partial x, \\partial f/\\partial y, \\partial f/\\partial z)$ — turns scalars into vector fields.\n- **Divergence** $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{F} = \\partial F_x/\\partial x + \\partial F_y/\\partial y + \\partial F_z/\\partial z$ — turns vector fields into scalars; \"outflow per unit volume\".\n- **Curl** $\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}$ — turns vector fields into vector fields; \"rotation per unit area\".\n\nThree integral theorems link these to integrals over boundaries:\n\n- **Green** (2D): $\\oint_{\\partial R} \\mathbf{F} \\cdot d\\mathbf{r} = \\iint_R (\\partial F_2/\\partial x - \\partial F_1/\\partial y)\\,dA$.\n- **Stokes** (general): $\\oint_{\\partial S} \\mathbf{F} \\cdot d\\mathbf{r} = \\iint_S (\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}) \\cdot d\\mathbf{S}$.\n- **Divergence**: $\\iiint_V \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{F}\\,dV = \\iint_{\\partial V} \\mathbf{F} \\cdot d\\mathbf{S}$.\n\nEach says: **integrating a derivative over a region equals integrating the original quantity over the boundary.** They generalise the fundamental theorem of calculus to higher dimensions.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 13,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Gradient as a vector field [S+N]\n\nFor $f(x, y) = x^2 + y^2$, the gradient is $\\nabla f = (2x, 2y)$ — radial, pointing outward.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "f_scalar : x^2 + y^2$\ngrad_f : [diff(f_scalar, x), diff(f_scalar, y)]$\nprint(\"∇f =\")$\ngrad_f;\n\nax_draw2d(\n  ax_vector_field(grad_f[1], grad_f[2], x, -2, 2, y, -2, 2),\n  title=\"∇(x² + y²) — radial outward field\",\n  xlabel=\"x\", ylabel=\"y\",\n  aspect_ratio=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 14,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "∇f =\n[2*x,2*y]"
          ]
        },
