46792647,45.0,35.53767779197439,29.05460409907714,24.44395478041652,21.037511025421807,18.43494882292201,16.389540334034777,14.74356283647073,159.77514056883194,157.61986494804046,154.98310652189997,151.69924423399362,147.52880770915152,142.12501634890182,135.00000000000003,125.5376777919744,113.19859051364821,98.130102354156,81.86989764584402,66.80140948635179,54.462322208025604,45.0,37.87498365109819,32.47119229084848,28.300755766006368,25.016893478100016,22.380135051959556,20.22485943116807,154.65382405805332,152.10272896905238,149.03624346792648,145.30484646876604,140.71059313749964,135.0,127.8749836510982,119.05460409907715,108.43494882292202,96.34019174590992,83.6598082540901,71.56505117707798,60.945395900922854,52.1250163489018,45.0,39.28940686250034,34.69515353123397,30.963756532073518,27.89727103094762,25.346175941946683,149.93141717813756,147.0947570770121,143.7461622625552,139.7636416907262,135.0,129.28940686250036,122.47119229084849,114.44395478041653,105.25511870305778,95.19442890773482,84.8055710922652,74.74488129694222,65.55604521958347,57.52880770915152,50.71059313749964,45.0,40.236358309273825,36.2538377374448,32.9052429229879,30.06858282186245,145.61965527615513,142.59464336859145,139.08561677997488,135.0,130.23635830927384,124.69515353123398,118.30075576600639,111.03751102542182,102.99461679191651,94.39870535499554,85.60129464500447,77.00538320808349,68.96248897457818,61.699244233993625,55.30484646876603,49.76364169072617,45.0,40.91438322002512,37.405356631408544,34.38034472384486,141.70983680775694,138.57633437499737,135.0,130.91438322002514,126.2538377374448,120.96375653207353,115.01689347810003,108.43494882292202,101.30993247402021,93.81407483429035,86.18592516570965,78.69006752597979,71.56505117707799,64.98310652189998,59.03624346792648,53.7461622625552,49.08561677997487,45.0,41.42366562500264,38.29016319224305,138.17983011986422,135.0,131.42366562500266,127.40535663140855,122.9052429229879,117.89727103094764,112.38013505195958,106.38954033403479,100.00797980144134,93.3664606634298,86.63353933657021,79.99202019855866,73.61045966596522,67.61986494804043,62.10272896905237,57.0947570770121,52.59464336859144,48.57633437499735,45.0,41.820169880135765,135.0,131.82016988013575,128.29016319224309,124.38034472384487,120.06858282186245,115.3461759419467,110.22485943116808,104.74356283647074,98.9726266148964,93.01278750418334,86.98721249581666,81.0273733851036,75.25643716352927,69.77514056883193,64.65382405805332,59.93141717813755,55.619655276155136,51.709836807756936,48.17983011986424,45.0]},\"showlegend\":false,\"hoverinfo\":\"skip\"}],\"layout\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"∇(x² + y²) — radial outward field\"},\"width\":700,\"height\":700,\"plot_bgcolor\":\"white\",\"paper_bgcolor\":\"white\",\"xaxis\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"x\"},\"gridcolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linecolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linewidth\":1,\"zerolinecolor\":\"black\",\"zerolinewidth\":1},\"yaxis\":{\"title\":{\"text\":\"y\"},\"scaleanchor\":\"x\",\"scaleratio\":1,\"gridcolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linecolor\":\"#ddd\",\"linewidth\":1,\"zerolinecolor\":\"black\",\"zerolinewidth\":1}}}"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Divergence\n\n$\\nabla \\cdot (x, y) = 2$ — a uniform outflow. $\\nabla \\cdot (-y, x) = 0$ — pure rotation, no outflow. Maxima symbolically:\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "F_radial : [x, y]$\nF_rotation : [-y, x]$\ndiv_radial : diff(F_radial[1], x) + diff(F_radial[2], y)$\ndiv_rot : diff(F_rotation[1], x) + diff(F_rotation[2], y)$\nprint(\"∇·(x, y) =\", div_radial)$\nprint(\"∇·(-y, x) =\", div_rot)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 15,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "∇·(x, y) = 2\n∇·(-y, x) = 0"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Curl in 3D\n\n$\\nabla \\times (-y, x, 0) = (0, 0, 2)$ — pure z-axis rotation, as expected. The full curl formula in 3D is\n\n$$\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F} = \\begin{pmatrix} \\partial F_z / \\partial y - \\partial F_y / \\partial z \\\\ \\partial F_x / \\partial z - \\partial F_z / \\partial x \\\\ \\partial F_y / \\partial x - \\partial F_x / \\partial y \\end{pmatrix}.$$\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "F3 : [-y, x, 0]$\ncurl_F : [\n  diff(F3[3], y) - diff(F3[2], z),\n  diff(F3[1], z) - diff(F3[3], x),\n  diff(F3[2], x) - diff(F3[1], y)\n]$\nprint(\"∇ × (-y, x, 0) =\")$\ncurl_F;",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 16,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "∇ × (-y, x, 0) ="
          ]
        },
        {
          "data": {
            "text/latex": [
              "\\left[ 0 , 0 , 2 \\right] "
            ]
          },
          "execution_count": 16,
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "execute_result"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Verifying Green's theorem [S+N]\n\nGreen: $\\oint_{\\partial R} (P\\,dx + Q\\,dy) = \\iint_R \\left(\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}\\right) dA$.\n\nTake $P = -y/2$, $Q = x/2$, $R$ = unit disc. Then $\\partial Q/\\partial x - \\partial P/\\partial y = 1$, so the area integral equals $\\mathrm{area}(R) = \\pi$. The line integral around the unit circle parameterised as $(\\cos t, \\sin t)$, $t \\in [0, 2\\pi]$:\n\n$$\\oint = \\int_0^{2\\pi} \\left( -\\tfrac{1}{2}\\sin t \\cdot (-\\sin t) + \\tfrac{1}{2}\\cos t \\cdot \\cos t \\right) dt = \\int_0^{2\\pi} \\tfrac{1}{2}\\,dt = \\pi.$$\n\nBoth sides $= \\pi$. Maxima confirms.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "P_g : -y/2$\nQ_g : x/2$\n\n/* RHS: area integral of dQ/dx - dP/dy over unit disc, in polar */\nintegrand_xy : diff(Q_g, x) - diff(P_g, y)$\nintegrand_polar : subst([x = r*cos(theta), y = r*sin(theta)], integrand_xy)$\nprint(\"∂Q/∂x - ∂P/∂y =\", integrand_xy)$\nRHS : integrate(integrate(integrand_polar * r, r, 0, 1), theta, 0, 2*%pi)$\nprint(\"RHS area integral =\", RHS)$\n\n/* LHS: line integral around unit circle */\nP_t : subst([x = cos(t), y = sin(t)], P_g)$\nQ_t : subst([x = cos(t), y = sin(t)], Q_g)$\nLHS : integrate(P_t * (-sin(t)) + Q_t * cos(t), t, 0, 2*%pi)$\nprint(\"LHS line integral =\", LHS)$\nprint(\"Match:\", is(equal(ratsimp(LHS - RHS), 0)))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 17,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "∂Q/∂x - ∂P/∂y = 1\nRHS area integral = %pi\nLHS line integral = %pi\nMatch: true"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "So $(P, Q) = (-y/2, x/2)$ gives a vector field whose line integral around any closed curve equals the *area* enclosed. That's a beautiful trick (and the basis of planimeters — mechanical devices that compute area by tracing a boundary).\n\n## The divergence theorem [S+N]\n\nDivergence theorem: $\\iiint_V (\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{F})\\,dV = \\iint_{\\partial V} \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\,dS$.\n\nTake $\\mathbf{F}(x, y, z) = (x, y, z)$ and $V$ = unit ball. Then $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{F} = 3$, so the volume integral is $3 \\cdot \\text{vol}(V) = 3 \\cdot 4\\pi/3 = 4\\pi$. The boundary integral over the unit sphere is $\\iint \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\,dS = \\iint 1 \\cdot dS = $ area of sphere = $4\\pi$. (On the unit sphere, $\\mathbf{F} = (x,y,z)$ equals the outward normal $\\mathbf{n}$, so $\\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} = 1$.)\n\nBoth sides are $4\\pi$. Verify the volume integral with Maxima.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "F_vec : [x, y, z]$\ndiv_F : diff(F_vec[1], x) + diff(F_vec[2], y) + diff(F_vec[3], z)$\nprint(\"∇·F =\", div_F)$\n\n/* Volume integral over unit ball, in spherical */\nV_int : integrate(integrate(integrate(3 * rho^2 * sin(phi),\n                                       rho, 0, 1),\n                              phi, 0, %pi),\n                    theta, 0, 2*%pi)$\nprint(\"∫∫∫ ∇·F dV =\", V_int)$\nprint(\"4π =\", float(4*%pi))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 18,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "∇·F = 3\n∫∫∫ ∇·F dV = 4*%pi\n4π = 12.566370614359172"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Why the integral theorems unify the subject\n\nA single line:\n\n$$\\int_M d\\omega = \\int_{\\partial M} \\omega.$$\n\nThis is the **generalised Stokes theorem** (in differential-geometric form). It encompasses:\n\n- The fundamental theorem of calculus ($\\int_a^b f' = f(b) - f(a)$),\n- Green's theorem,\n- Stokes' theorem in $\\mathbb{R}^3$,\n- The divergence theorem,\n- Gauss-Bonnet (for 2-manifolds),\n- ...\n\nEvery one of these has the same shape: integrate a derivative over a region = integrate the original over the boundary. The differential form $\\omega$ and exterior derivative $d$ make this rigorous; what we computed above are the classical incarnations.\n\n## What we have at the end of Stage 2\n\nVector calculus closes the multivariable picture:\n\n- **Topology** (notebook 1) gave us the right notion of \"near\" and \"compact\".\n- **Continuity** (notebook 2) revealed why limits along all paths matter.\n- **Differentiation** (notebook 3) replaced the slope with a Jacobian.\n- **Inverse/implicit function theorems** (notebook 4) said the Jacobian's invertibility controls local behaviour.\n- **Multiple integration** (notebook 5) generalised the Riemann construction.\n- **Vector calculus** (this notebook) tied derivatives and integrals back together.\n\nStage 3 leaves $\\mathbb{R}^n$ for $\\mathbb{C}$. The two-dimensional structure of $\\mathbb{C}$ + a multiplication law is enormously more rigid than $\\mathbb{R}^2$ alone — and unlocks tools (residues, conformal maps) without any analogue in real analysis.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    }
  ]
}